    "capabilities": ["IOS", "ANDROID"],
    "isDefault": false,
    "forms": {
        "$comment": "Managed-form kinds, formKey -> kind (append-only vocabulary: RSVP | LEAD | MAILING_LIST | PROOFING). Compose stamps these into repobot.deploy.json as formKinds; the dashboard renders declared kinds as typed views and keeps the raw Inbox for undeclared keys.",
        "booking-request": "LEAD"
    },
    "theme": {
        "$comment": "The warm-boutique register's brand overlay: a fresh herbal green over the register's cream warmth — the clean-and-natural voice for a home-services subscription, deliberately apart from the trades register the category's other starters wear. Marketing pages resolve brand over preset accent, so the overlay re-skins the pages and the app surfaces together.",
        "brand": {
            "primary": "#2f7a52",
            "primaryDark": "#8fd6ae"
        }
    },
    "contentContract": {
        "$comment": "The pack's content slots, as data (packs/README.md 'Content contract'). Declares what a composer (agent or tool) must bind for a generated variant of this pack to present as real: slot paths into the typed content module, their kinds, and minimums. The demo business is a home cleaner, but the slots are trade-agnostic — lawn care, pool service, or pest control binds the same shape. The home page's middle is either/or: the turnover story (turnover.steps + roomReady.items — the base demo and both remixes, retraded as a season rail and a treatment rail) or the classic subscription trio (included + gallery + metrics) — each of those collections is min 0 because the builders drop an empty section, and the pack's content tests require one story or the other in full. specimens (the portrait board, the pest remix's creature index) is optional on either story. Authored alongside the module and guarded by the pack's content tests — the module satisfies the contract; the contract never drifts ahead of it.",
        "module": "web/app/src/View/ServicesRecurring/content.ts",
